    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1333">

                <pb facs="0898" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/108.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Special Agent Carothers.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 15, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Bevan, Tampico, reports General Peláez, assuming to represent Villa, has demanded
                    fifty thousand pesos of Penn Mex. Oil Co., American corporation.</p>
                <pb facs="0899" n="783" xml:id="pg783"/>
                <p>Request Villa inform you whether Peláez is bona fide representative and if so to
                    order him withdraw this demand.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
